sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, ADR 0241 allowlists, DECISIONS R1-R4 + 5 (process.stop shape, shared SSH identity). Same shape as firewall.allow.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-03, rule 22 (no script: one ufw argv per change over @swamp/ssh exec; a typed step plans positions, Lab #4334).
  %% status: reviewed
  %% command: firewall:remove
  %% kind: firewall.remove
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Target Node<br/>reached over ssh
  CLI->>GW: firewall:remove 5432<br/>--node=7
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit firewall:remove 5432 --node=7`
  %%> - syntax: `<port> --node=ID [--from=SOURCE] [--protocol=tcp|udp]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the port as the argument, and the Node
  %%> - `--from` and `--protocol` only when several rules share the port
  %%> Confirmation:
  %%> - the CLI asks before removal; `--yes` confirms without a prompt
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI and the MCP tool send the same request
  Note over GW: Validate, mark removing<br/>rule: removing · task #5131
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to Node 7
  %%> - exactly one rule on Node 7 matches the port, source and protocol
  %%> - no other firewall change runs on Node 7; the Gateway holds one lock per Node
  %%> Works out what to keep:
  %%> - a ufw line that another rule, or a rule Orbit itself needs, also uses stays on the Node
  %%> - only lines that belong to this rule alone are removed
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the rule for port 5432 recorded as removing
  %%> - task #5131 recorded with the full intent
  %%> - nothing has happened on the Node yet
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-firewall-direct
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the ufw lines to remove, and the lines that must stay
  %%> - Node 7's address and SSH host keys; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5131
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  SW->>N: Read the rules<br/>ufw status · @swamp/ssh exec
  %%> How:
  %%> - Swamp reaches Node 7 over SSH from 209 with the official `@swamp/ssh` behavior
  %%> - refuses an inactive firewall (`firewall.backend_inactive`) before any change
  Note over SW: Plan the changes<br/>typed step on 209
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - turns ufw's numbered rows into the ufw commands this rule needs, in order
  %%> - an insert position counts the rows as they will be after the earlier commands
  %%> Why typed, not cfgmgmt:
  %%> - `@swamp/cfgmgmt/firewall` cannot insert at a position (Lab #4334) or name a port range
  SW->>N: Change the rules<br/>one ufw argv · @swamp/ssh exec
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - deletes each line that belongs to this rule alone; a line that is already gone is skipped
  %%> - a line that a role also needs (`retain`) stays
  %%> - runs the planned commands one at a time; nothing is copied to the Node
  SW->>N: Read the result<br/>ufw status · @swamp/ssh exec
  Note over SW: Check the rules<br/>typed step on 209
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - checks every removed line is gone, and retained lines are still there
  %%> - prints the public result; a line that ufw changed in between fails the check, and a rerun repairs it
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the rule only counts as removed when ufw shows it
  alt end state is right
    N-->>SW: end state confirmed
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the check passed
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Delete the rule<br/>record gone · task succeeded
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the rule for port 5432 is deleted from the Gateway
    %%> - task #5131 succeeds
  else removing or checking fails
    N--xSW: exit ≠ 0
    %%> When:
    %%> - ufw refuses the change, SSH fails, or the end state is wrong
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its error code
    Note over GW: Mark the rule failed<br/>task failed · rerun after a fix
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the rule for port 5432 stays, marked failed, so you can see it
    %%> - task #5131 fails
    %%> On the Node:
    %%> - lines removed before the failure stay removed; there is no rollback
    %%> - that is safe: a rerun skips lines that are already gone
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5131
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
